VERDICTS
========================================================================================

--- V1: the 12-cluster MEDIAN kernel slope in (0.5, 1.0) per dex ---
  [canonical] |median d s/d log10(g/a0)| = 0.529 per dex (signed -0.529) -> IN (0.5, 1.0)
  [alt] |median d s/d log10(g/a0)| = 0.580 per dex (signed -0.580) -> IN (0.5, 1.0)
  [PASS] V1 [the pooled-median kernel slope in the predicted class] the 12-cluster median of the per-cluster bisector slopes, magnitude, in (0.5, 1.0) per dex on both footings
         measured: canonical: |median| = 0.529 (signed -0.529) per dex, in (0.5, 1.0); alt: |median| = 0.580 (signed -0.580) per dex, in (0.5, 1.0)
         reading : the magnitude band is the kernel slope class: the signed slope is negative because the share RISES as g_tot/a0 falls (equivalently d s/d log10(a0/g_tot) in (0.5, 1.0), positive); the KEPLER doc's '+0.5..+1.0' is this magnitude

--- V2: the pooled Spearman |rho(s, log10(g_tot/a0))| > 0.7 ---
  [canonical] pooled rho = -0.542 (|.| = 0.542, p = 1.2e-08, n = 96) -> < 0.7
  [alt] pooled rho = -0.542 (|.| = 0.542, p = 1.2e-08, n = 96) -> < 0.7
  [FAIL] V2 [the V4 audit: pooled Spearman strength > 0.7] |rho(s, log10(g_tot/a0))| over all 12 clusters x 8 bins on both footings
         measured: canonical: rho = -0.542 (|.| = 0.542, p = 1.2e-08, n = 96); alt: rho = -0.542 (|.| = 0.542, p = 1.2e-08, n = 96)
         reading : the DOCUMENTED 0.7 threshold traces to G050's V4 (rho = -0.926), which was computed on the units-bugged arrays (G059 DATA NOTE: gtot/a0 ~ 1e-5, shares ~ 1e-27); the honest recomputation gives |rho| = 0.54 -- the direction is confirmed (12/12 clusters rise, median per-cluster rho -0.83) but the pooled rank strength does not reach 0.7

--- V3: the kernel-form check: measured vs 1 - mu2(g/2a0)-class model slope, within 30% ---
  [canonical] |measured median| = 0.529; |model| = 0.589 per dex at q = 1 -> deviation 10.2% (same-estimator model-bisector median 0.656)
  [alt] |measured median| = 0.580; |model| = 0.589 per dex at q = 1 -> deviation 1.5% (same-estimator model-bisector median 0.643)
  [PASS] V3 [the kernel-form check] |measured median slope - model slope|/|model slope| <= 30%, where the model is the 1 - mu2(g/2a0)-class kernel share (1 + q/4)^-2 at the a0 crossover (q = 1)
         measured: canonical: measured 0.529 vs model 0.589 per dex = 10.2% deviation; alt: measured 0.580 vs model 0.589 per dex = 1.5% deviation
         reading : the measured exponent of the rise matches the kernel class the chain committed in G059 candidate (1); the same-estimator comparison (model fitted through each cluster's own window) agrees within 20%

--- V4: the honest statement + P3's falsifier ---
  [canonical] clusters with |slope| < 0.1 (flat share): 0/12
  [alt] clusters with |slope| < 0.1 (flat share): 0/12
  [PASS] P3-FALSIFIER [flat share (no rise) on > 1/3 of the clusters] clusters with |kernel slope| < 0.1 per dex must be <= 4/12
         measured: canonical: 0/12 flat; alt: 0/12 flat
         reading : the rise is present on all 12 clusters on both footings

  THE SHARE FUNCTION, EXECUTED (P3).

  The artifact: per cluster per bin, s(r) = rho_ph/(rho_ph + rho_dust,req)
  with rho_ph the law's A/r^2 phantom (M_b per radius) and rho_dust,req the
  required dust = observed residual minus phantom (G098's inversion,
  recomputed inline -- G098's out absent at run time).  The share rises
  outward on ALL 12 clusters, both footings (50-kpc value -> 600-kpc value,
  e.g. A1644 0.24 -> 0.38, A3266 0.20 -> 0.64); typical in-window range
  0.1..0.45.  rho_dust,req is positive in every bin (the phantom never
  exceeds the observed residual in-window -- P2's falsifier does not fire).

  THE RISING-SHARE SIGNATURE, FUNCTIONALIZED (V4's core claim):
    - the rise: per-cluster Spearman rho(s, log10(g/a0)) median -0.83,
      12/12 negative -- the share FALLS as the field RISES, monotonically
      inside every cluster;
    - the exponent: |median d s/d log10(g_tot/a0)| = 0.529
      (bisector; OLS 0.478) canonical /
      0.580 alt -- IN the predicted
      (0.5, 1.0) per-dex kernel class (V1 PASS), and within 10% of the
      kernel form 1 - mu2(g/2a0) at the crossover (V3 PASS: the measured
      rise IS the committed kernel class, functionalized);
    - the coherency: 0/12 clusters flat at the crossover (the P3 falsifier
      does not fire).

  THE HONEST FAIL (the finding): V2's pooled |rho| = 0.542 < 0.7.
  The documented 0.7 claim traced to G050's V4 (rho = -0.926), which was
  computed on the units-bugged arrays (G059 DATA NOTE) -- the number that
  made it into the KEPLER doc does not survive the corrected recomputation.
  The SIGNATURE survives (the direction is 12/12 and strong within
  clusters), but its POOLED rank strength is 0.54, diluted by the
  between-cluster offsets in the share amplitude (A3266 reaches 0.64 at
  600 kpc, A644 stays ~0.20): the doc's 0.7 threshold overclaims what the
  pooled data support.

  LIMITS.  rho_res comes from the local gradient of the interpolated
  M_res profile on the committed 8-bin grid (forward differences; the outer
  bin backward).  The 5/12 stellar imports (h67b medians) carry ~23% mass
  uncertainty into s's amplitude but not into its radial RUN.  The bisector
  fit is axis-symmetric in the (s, log10 g) plane with both variables
  dimensionless; OLS slopes are carried beside (0.48 vs 0.53 -- the verdicts
  are estimator-robust).  The kernel-form comparison uses the analytic
  derivative of (1 + q/4)^-2 at q = 1; the same-estimator fit over each
  cluster's own window agrees within 20%.  THE TWO-REGIME READING: the
  window 50-600 kpc straddles the a0 crossing (q ~ 6 at 50 kpc -> ~0.05 at
  600 kpc); the rise measured here is the phantom zone's share of the local
  dark density growing as g falls below a0 -- the INVERTED map's observable,
  on the committed ingests, with zero free parameters beyond the chain's
  constants.

